MD Manager work arrives as slice PRDs in `docs/` (PRD_CHALLENGE_DAY2.md → PRD_SLICE2.md → PRD_SLICE3.md). Slice 2 (read-only view, `GET /api/file`) shipped 2026-09-19 (`docs/HANDOFF_SLICE2.md`). Slice 3 (CodeMirror editor, `PUT /api/file`, `POST /api/mutate`, operation dialogs) was implemented 2026-09-20 with evidence in `docs/HANDOFF_SLICE3.md`; commits were left to the user.

**Why:** The PRDs require Red → Green → Refactor per increment with observed failing-test evidence, one Playwright worker, `scratch-*` fixture artifacts cleaned in afterEach, and a final fixture-cleanliness gate. Test-authoring mistakes must be listed separately from product Reds.

**How to apply:** Run browser tests on free ports (`MD_MANAGER_WEB_PORT=5184 MD_MANAGER_API_PORT=3014`; dev servers usually occupy 5173/3001) and never run the unit suite concurrently with the browser suite (the committed-fixture listing test sees scratch files). Known traps: React StrictMode resets refs on remount; editor text must flow editor→session only (sync back only on an explicit generation change, in a layout effect); native `<dialog>` must be closed in a layout-effect cleanup to restore focus; extra UI rows above the graph shrink the canvas and make off-screen node clicks fail; Vite dev 404s malformed percent-encoded URLs before the SPA loads (a middleware in vite.config.ts serves the shell).
